1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,060
I would like to understand why, again, you think that men benefit from feminism more?

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:09,040
I wouldn't really argue that men in general have benefited from feminism more than women.

3
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:15,340
I would argue that a tiny minority of people who happen to be mostly men have benefited from feminism more than women.

4
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:18,280
And they are capitalists and dark-tetrid men.

5
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:25,020
While I'm in total agreement with feminists that women have indeed faced many historical injustices throughout history,

6
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:30,000
where I tend to disagree with them is the true reason why women are much freer today.

7
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:32,980
I don't think traditional feminism alone deserves the credit.

8
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:39,180
I strongly believe that technology and the exchange of ideas between cultures were the primary drivers.

9
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:44,020
Technologies like the washing machine, the dishwasher and reliable bath control

10
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:47,620
reduced domestic burden and gave women better control,

11
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:51,440
making careers and education far more accessible.

12
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:54,380
And at the same time, as societies interacted,

13
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:58,540
harmful practices such as female genital mutilation and child marriage

14
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:04,620
increasingly came under challenge from ideas centered on individual freedom and human rights.

15
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:09,100
Let me now explain to you how feminism benefits men more than it does women.

16
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:12,940
Expanding paid employment of women increased labor supply,

17
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:17,300
which all else equal exerts a downward pressure on wages.

18
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:22,120
And capitalists, who are mostly men, benefited from a larger pool of workers,

19
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:27,620
a higher labor force participation, and weakened bargaining power of the existing workforce.

20
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:33,100
In other words, feminism made the rich, who are mostly men, even more richer.

21
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:38,700
And secondly, sex positivity messaging, which frames casual sex as liberating for women,

22
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:43,540
increases the supply of short-term mating opportunities. This disproportionately

23
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:48,480
benefits men who tend to score higher in what we call sociosexuality, in other words,

24
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:53,900
willingness to participate in non-committal sex. The average woman, as we know, is less oriented

25
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:59,380
toward and less psychologically rewarded by casual sex. This is indicated by the fact that women

26
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:05,740
report substantially lower rates of orgasm in casual sex compared to men. Men report 80 to 90

27
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:10,840
percent rates of orgasm in casual sex compared to women 30 to 40 percent.
